= Conclusion

The pipeline reaches mean mask IoU $0.921$ and mean boundary $F_1$ $0.432$ across the $55$-frame hand-labeled subset spanning eleven distinct VARTM infusion runs. The two reimplemented prior classical-CV pipelines reach IoU $0.144$ (Lekanidis and Vosniakos 2020) and $0.075$ (Almazán-Lázaro 2022) on the same subset. The per-sample component-removal ablation shows the integrated configuration's headline IoU surviving the removal of any single primitive with margins under $0.02$, the largest being the darken-only clip at $-0.018$. Camera-shift registration remains opt-in because enabling it on the mechanically-stable videos triggers unwanted phase-correlation refits rather than absorbing real motion. The regime-indexed configuration lookup translates the per-sample evidence into preprocessing settings keyed to the run circumstances a practitioner can read off their own bench. Aggregated across the eleven samples, the pipeline runs at $21$ frames per second on a single CPU process and at $207$ frames per second on a single CUDA device, a $10$-fold speedup at matched parameter values.
